title: vera_intro_beat2
---
PRACTITIONER: Don't. Please — don't call it in yet.
REID: I'm not Bureau.
PRACTITIONER: You were. It's in how you came through the door.
REID: Someone's paying me to find you. That's all this is.
PRACTITIONER: The creditor.
REID: You know how this goes, then.
PRACTITIONER: I know how it's supposed to go. I file, I work, I pay. That's the whole arrangement.
PRACTITIONER: I stopped being able to work.
REID: Grade II doesn't just stop.
PRACTITIONER: No. It doesn't.
PRACTITIONER: It drains while I'm asleep. I wake up and there's less of me. Not tired. Less.
PRACTITIONER: Four assessments. Every one came back inside tolerance.
REID: When did it start?
PRACTITIONER: After I tried to stop using it.
PRACTITIONER: I didn't know how to say that to anyone. It sounds like a person making excuses.
PRACTITIONER: It still does. I can hear it.
REID: Stay here. Don't go out the front.
PRACTITIONER: You're not calling it in.
REID: I'm deciding.
<<show_narration "I'd heard a hundred people lie about why they couldn't pay. None of them had ever gotten the details wrong in that particular direction.">>
<<set $beat2_vera_spoken = true>>
===
